2	\N	545947	27559	After KING’s death, CHOI decides to destroy the phoenix hairpin as instructed by KWOK.  Unwilling to see KING’s efforts go to waste, WAN means to injure herself.  KWOK gives the phoenix hairpin to CHENG, and WAN begins to worry about the lady and her son.  HA purposely fights with WAN for the custody of HO as her apprentice.  As KWOK is about to start her plot against YI, the news that YI has fallen from a tree arrives.  YI suffers from head injury and seems to have developed some kind of mental problem.  KWOK allows YI to recuperate at the Taoist Temple, but not in the company of CHENG.  HA points out that CHENG and YI are separated by the phoenix hairpin and that it is WAN who has dragged them into trouble.  She ridicules WAN for being too selfish and making others suffer while WAN does not say a word to defend herself.  HO goes to see YI off, which touches him considerably.… ...	\N	Episode 2	https://vidsrc.to/embed/tv/16209/1/2
3	\N	545948	27559	KWOK needs HO to explain the design of the clothing, making HA and WAN believe that the Empress is going to punish the girl.  To everyone’s surprise and delight, KWOK appreciates HO’s design and holds it in high regard.  Chief General MA YUEN-CHI is no longer trusted by the Emperor after making a mistake.  CHEUNG who is deemed to be in the same league with him is also embroiled in the matter.  Except for HO, all the imperial servants have been avoiding CHEUNG.  CHENG’s health is deteriorating and YI is finally allowed to return to the Palace to see his mother.  LING and FEI-YIN pick a row over trivial matters, causing HO to accidentally damage Lady WONG’s new dress.  HO has no choice but to alter the dress design.  KWOK flies into a rage after knowing this.  To defend HO, HA shifts the blame onto WAN emphasizing that it is all a trap set by her.  LING and HO meet up at night but get caught by YIN midway through their gathering.… ...	\N	Episode 3	https://vidsrc.to/embed/tv/16209/1/3
